==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|knobelouch}}, with dissimilation from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|chlobalouh}}. The latter part of the word is, of course, {{m|de|Lauch||leek}}. The first part originally pertains to {{m|de|klieben||to cleave}}, but was later adapted to the large group of terms for thick objects beginning with ''kn-'' (cf. {{m|de|Knopf}}, {{m|de|Knoten}}, {{m|de|Knolle}}, etc.). The same in {{cog|nl|knoflook}}.

